%description:

Tcp.keepAliveEnabled:on-busy -- during a transfer longer than the idle time no probe goes; the first comes the idle time after the last ACK.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "keepalive (RFC 9293 section 3.8.4): after keepAliveIdleTime
without a received segment and without data in flight, send a probe"; MUST-26: "Keep-alive
packets MUST only be sent when no sent data is outstanding".

The class on-busy: TcpAlgorithmBase::processKeepAliveTimer() starts the idle time again when
data is in flight or waits. This facet comes from the coverage gap loop: no test reached the code of this part. This test separates "on" from "off", where no probe comes.

Host under test: host1, with an idle time of 1 s (precondition); the network is
TapRouterNetwork with a bottleneck of 10 Mbps, and host1 sends 5000000 bytes at 0.2 s, which
take about 4 s. Observation: level 1, the first probe comes 1 s after the ACK of all data.

%# parameter: Tcp.keepAliveEnabled
%# class: on-busy
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.keepAliveEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpKeepAliveEnabledOnBusy")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackNo == {isn} + 1 + 5000000")
             .describe("the ACK of all data of host1")
             .within(10.0))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
              .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 5000000 && pk.dataLength <= tcp.headerLength")
              .describe("an early keepalive probe")
              .within(0.9))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false && tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 5000000 && pk.dataLength <= tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("keepalive probe")
             .within(0.2));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpKeepAliveEnabledOnBusy compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.keepAliveEnabled = true    # the parameter under test
network = inet.protocoltest.TapRouterNetwork
*.bottleneckDatarate = 10Mbps
*.host1.tcp.keepAliveIdleTime = 1s
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 5000000B
*.host1.app[0].tClose = 10000s
sim-time-limit = 20s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpKeepAliveEnabledOnBusy: PASS
